{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevG7NkxVb5tWN2ruDqLJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. I have a clear understanding of the codebase. Let me document my findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:9-14` - Shipment data class with status enum\n- `ShipmentStatus enum (Shipment.kt:23-27)` - CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED states\n- `InMemoryShipmentRepository` - Has save(), findById(), existsById() methods\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-44` - POST /shipments creates CREATED shipments\n- `ApiExceptions.kt` - ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409) patterns\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` - Error codes enum\n\n**Conventions in this API:**\n- Exceptions are thrown, not HTTP status codes assembled in controllers\n- All errors use the envelope: `{error: {code, message, fields}}`\n- Tests verify both HTTP status AND error body structure\n- Repository provides simple save/find operations; business logic is in controller\n\n**Affected files and why they cannot be avoided:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - Must add the confirm endpoint and logic\n2. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Must add tests for new endpoint (acceptance criterion 3, 5)\n3. `ApiError.kt` - Must add error code for invalid state rejection (409 for CANCELLED case)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Idempotency: confirming CONFIRMED must not fail; must handle current state properly\n- Error codes: need to add a new one to the enum (requires ApiError.kt edit)\n- Breaking existing tests if repository or model contract changes\n\n**Open questions:** None identified. The ticket is clear on all business cases.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to enum for when confirming a non-CREATED shipment (specifically CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add method:\n   ```\n   POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm\n   - Find shipment by ID; throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) if not found (404)\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, return it unchanged (idempotent retry succeeds)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, ...) (409)\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED via repository.save(), return updated shipment\n   - Return ResponseEntity.ok(shipment)\n   ```\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add tests:\n   - `confirm a created shipment moves it to CONFIRMED` - POST, verify status changed, 200 OK\n   - `confirm a confirmed shipment succeeds and changes nothing` - POST twice, both succeed, no change\n   - `confirm a cancelled shipment is rejected with 409` - Create CANCELLED directly in repo, POST confirm, 409 with error code\n   - `confirm a non-existent shipment is rejected with 404` - POST to missing ID, 404 with error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- *Put new logic in a service class*: The existing controller-only design works fine for this simple state transition. Adding a service layer would be unrelated refactoring (scope violation).\n- *Using a generic ConflictException without error code*: The existing code pattern (ConflictException takes an ErrorCode) requires adding the code. Not adding it would be inconsistent.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | repository.findById(id) | repository.save(shipment.copy(status=CONFIRMED)) | 200 OK with updated Shipment | Normal path |\n| CONFIRMED retry | repository.findById(id) | none | 200 OK with unchanged Shipment | Early return if status == CONFIRMED |\n| CANCELLED | repository.findById(id) | none | 409 Conflict | throw ConflictException |\n| Not found | repository.findById(id) returns null | none | 404 Not Found | throw ResourceNotFoundException |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `confirms a created shipment and returns it` - Happy path: verify CREATED→CONFIRMED transition and 200 status\n2. `confirming a confirmed shipment succeeds without change` - Idempotency: call twice, verify second succeeds and status unchanged\n3. `rejects confirmation of a cancelled shipment with the error envelope` - Error case: 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n4. `rejects confirmation of a non-existent shipment with the error envelope` - Error case: 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1997,"cache_read_input_tokens":16106,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1997},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8b58b4c-47a3-432f-a548-fe46eaa71e69","uuid":"49c95590-bcbf-450f-a7da-b0f5579f9a15","timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:50:53.688Z","request_id":"req_011CevG7MwbgsupB4atNKwRv"}
